  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) is the best so far at 0.688 acc / 0.659 F1, confirming that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + scvi_n200 + concat fusion is a strong recipe. However, the image encoder remains at resnet50, which performed very poorly as image-only (0.208 acc), suggesting the image modality may be underutilized. Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially larger, ImageNet-pretrained ViT) meaningfully improve multimodal performance while keeping all other winning settings fixed? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the single highest-impact untested axis in the context of our top configuration. The image encoder is a major design lever with only one option (resnet50) explored in the multiprofile multimodal regime, and the weak image-only baseline hints that a stronger encoder could unlock additional signal. Testing config_038 isolates the image-encoder effect cleanly, reducing uncertainty about whether to invest further in image quality or pivot to other axes (fusion type, scgpt RNA encoder)."
}

